WEBVTT

00:00:00.501 --> 00:00:02.418
- Previously on The O.C.:
- What? You're driving.

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:04.295
Yeah, because you're drunk.

00:00:05.587 --> 00:00:09.339
- Stop, okay? You're scaring me.
- Good. You're scaring me.

00:00:09.548 --> 00:00:10.757
I called the therapist.

00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:12.508
- Mom.
- She's right, kiddo.

00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:14.926
Therapy was part of the deal
of you moving in.

00:00:15.135 --> 00:00:16.969
I know you. You go to Harbor, right?

00:00:17.178 --> 00:00:18.637
- Marissa Cooper.
- What's wrong with you?

00:00:18.804 --> 00:00:21.013
Your sister,
do you ever hear from her?

00:00:21.222 --> 00:00:23.098
The number I have
is no longer in service.

00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.099
I like you. So does she.

00:00:25.516 --> 00:00:28.727
- Lf we don't put an end to this soon...
- Someone's gonna get hurt.

00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:36.231
So maybe next time
we go see a movie...

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:38.816
...it won't be a three-hour
period piece about boats.

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:40.817
They call them ships. And I liked it.

00:00:41.026 --> 00:00:43.903
I don't know. Russell Crowe,
he just doesn't do anything for me.

00:00:44.111 --> 00:00:46.446
I mean, people say
he's good-Iooking...

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:48.447
...but I don't see it.

00:00:48.656 --> 00:00:50.574
- I never really thought about it.
- Hey.

00:00:50.782 --> 00:00:52.908
Only one more day left in 2003.

00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:55.243
It's been a good year.

00:00:55.869 --> 00:01:00.080
Yes. My parents got divorced,
my dad went bankrupt...

00:01:00.913 --> 00:01:02.748
...and I OD'd.

00:01:03.832 --> 00:01:04.958
I meant...

00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.292
...for me.

00:01:07.751 --> 00:01:10.753
I know. I can't wait to celebrate
the new year...

00:01:10.961 --> 00:01:12.587
...with you.

00:01:14.422 --> 00:01:16.715
So, what do you wanna do?
I heard of some parties...

00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:20.467
Maybe we should take it easy
after what happened at Christmas.

00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:21.968
What happened at Christmas?

00:01:22.635 --> 00:01:25.470
It's all kind of a blur, actually.

00:01:26.805 --> 00:01:27.847
Kidding.

00:01:29.598 --> 00:01:31.307
Funny.

00:01:31.516 --> 00:01:32.975
I thought we could hang here.

00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:37.770
You know, maybe rent a couple
Russell Crowe movies.

00:01:40.313 --> 00:01:42.231
Stay in...

00:01:42.648 --> 00:01:44.316
...so I know you'll be safe.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.326
I love you.

00:02:09.373 --> 00:02:10.624
I mean...

00:02:10.832 --> 00:02:12.583
l... I didn't mean... I...

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.710
Thank you.

00:02:18.212 --> 00:02:20.088
You're welcome.

00:02:23.924 --> 00:02:26.300
Midnight. Curfew.

00:02:52.775 --> 00:02:54.234
I love you.

00:02:54.401 --> 00:02:55.402
I love you.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.278
How hard is that to say?

00:02:57.903 --> 00:02:59.071
Saying it's easy.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.322
Meaning it?

00:03:01.656 --> 00:03:03.407
That's the hard part.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:08.993
- Who the hell are you?
- It's a long story. Who the hell are you?

00:03:09.202 --> 00:03:11.745
It doesn't work that way, dude.
It's my pool house.

00:03:11.954 --> 00:03:13.913
Actually, dude, it's my pool house.

00:03:14.122 --> 00:03:15.581
So this is yours.

00:03:16.331 --> 00:03:17.791
You want it back?

00:03:17.957 --> 00:03:20.167
I got plenty, thanks.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.419
You're Kirsten's sister Hailey, right?

00:03:23.628 --> 00:03:27.088
So you've heard of me. I guess
Kirsten remembers I actually do exist.

00:03:27.297 --> 00:03:29.590
- She didn't say you were coming.
- She doesn't know.

00:03:29.798 --> 00:03:32.800
Look, we'll get it all
sorted out over breakfast.

00:03:33.008 --> 00:03:35.343
The living room couch
is pretty comfortable.

00:03:39.929 --> 00:03:41.389
And...

00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:42.639
...Iove you too.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.296
Hey.

00:04:33.505 --> 00:04:35.631
What happened to you?
Lady kick you to the curb?

00:04:35.839 --> 00:04:38.716
The pool house was occupied.
Your aunt.

00:04:38.925 --> 00:04:41.009
- Hailey's here? Awesome.
- Yeah, she's...

00:04:41.218 --> 00:04:44.511
Nine across, seven-letter word for...

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.597
Separate seats, you guys.
There's no sex in the champagne room.

00:04:47.805 --> 00:04:50.265
- Good morning to you too.
- Morning. Where's Hailey?

00:04:50.474 --> 00:04:55.226
- I don't know. Thailand. Morocco.
- I think she's planting trees in Tacoma.

00:04:55.435 --> 00:04:57.186
Costa Rica, building churches.

00:04:57.436 --> 00:04:59.604
I think it was Nicaragua,
and they were hospitals.

00:04:59.813 --> 00:05:03.190
- She's in the pool house.
- What are you talking about?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.108
Did you not notice Ryan
sleeping on the couch?

00:05:06.275 --> 00:05:08.110
Your sister's here.

00:05:08.318 --> 00:05:10.194
Wait, wait. You saw her...

00:05:10.403 --> 00:05:14.238
...you were talking to her, or...?
Did she say why she was here?

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:17.407
I have two guesses.
Either she's run out of money...

00:05:17.615 --> 00:05:18.991
...or she's run out of money.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.159
Three-letter word for hilarious?

00:05:21.368 --> 00:05:22.910
"Dad." Write that down.

00:05:23.077 --> 00:05:25.662
- She is probably out of money, though.
- Hailey's here.

00:05:27.205 --> 00:05:28.747
Hey, guys. Guess who's back.

00:05:28.956 --> 00:05:30.332
Hello, Hailey.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.167
Aunt Hailey.
Later, when you're dressed, we'll hug.

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:36.502
Seth. Robe. Her. Now.

00:05:39.546 --> 00:05:41.505
There you are.

00:05:41.714 --> 00:05:43.465
- Happy New Year, everyone.
- Happy New Year.

00:05:43.715 --> 00:05:45.258
Hi.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.093
We would have come
and picked you up...

00:05:48.301 --> 00:05:51.303
...at the airport or the train station.
- Or the border.

00:05:51.512 --> 00:05:54.263
Yeah, well, it was late,
and my cell phone got shut off.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:55.973
When you ran out of money?

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:59.683
So you're gonna stay with us.
For some time?

00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:06.855
I'm gonna make up the guest bedroom.
Bedding, sheets, now.

00:06:08.105 --> 00:06:12.233
Married 17 years, the first things that go
are the full sentences. Welcome back.

00:06:12.441 --> 00:06:13.984
Thanks.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.404
Looking good, nephew Seth.

00:06:19.613 --> 00:06:21.197
Thank you. Puberty happened.

00:06:21.405 --> 00:06:24.074
- It's been that long?
- It sure has. Be glad you missed it.

00:06:24.282 --> 00:06:26.033
Check this out though.

00:06:27.451 --> 00:06:29.786
Chest hair. And a new friend.

00:06:29.994 --> 00:06:31.912
Yeah, that's Ryan. He's...

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.663
He's kind of a long story.

00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:37.540
